<section class="faq section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div>
    <h2 id="faq-title">
      Frequently asked
      <br />
      questions
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details>
      <summary>
        What is Manvalan Finance?<span></span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          It’s a personal finance tracker for your everyday money. Record income
          and expenses, manage separate wallets, organize group ledgers, and
          keep track of money you lend or borrow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>
        Do I need an account or internet?<span></span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          No account needed. Your records are stored locally, and everyday
          tracking works offline. There’s no backend, telemetry, or automatic
          cloud sync.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>
        Does it connect to my bank?<span></span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          No. You add transactions yourself, so you stay in control of what you
          record. Bank imports and automatic bank connections aren’t part of the
          app.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>
        Can I track money I lend or borrow?<span></span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Yes. Record lent or borrowed amounts, add due dates, and track partial
          repayments or additional advances. Settled loans stay organized
          separately.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>
        What happens if I change phones?<span></span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Export a full JSON backup in Settings, keep it somewhere safe, and
          restore it on your new device. Back up before uninstalling: records
          don’t sync automatically. CSV exports are for reading, not restoring.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>
        Which devices can I use it on?<span></span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>
          Manavalan Finance is built for Android. Download the Android APK from
          the v2.0.0 release on GitHub. There isn’t a public iOS download here
          yet.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
